     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like it could be an error, so I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The maximum is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and **2000 mg/day** for extended-release. This order is about twice the immediate-release maximum, which raises the risk of severe stomach side effects and lactic acidosis.\n\n**Some possible intended orders:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum). Since 1700 = 2 \u00d7 850, this seems like the most likely mix-up.\n- **850 mg by mouth twice daily** (1700 mg total per day).\n- **1700 mg by mouth once or split per day**, if 1700 mg was meant as the daily total.\n\nWhich one did you mean? Also, should it be immediate-release or extended-release? Once you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add it as a note on the order."
      }
     ],
